  m_text: 'The grandeur of the peony has inspired poets and artists for centuries.
    Claude Monet painted peonies in his Giverny garden and Chinese poets immortalized
    the flower in verse as a metaphor for fleeting beauty and unearthly elegance.


    If
    you wish to do the same, click on the artist in the scene.


    If you want
    to see a gallery of peony art pieces, click on the canvas.'
